	(text "+3V3 comes from the FireBeetle regulator (PWR_FLAG). B1 plugs into the FireBeetle's own\nbattery socket (J3 is that socket, not a separate part)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 251.46 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6b752251-5674-41b4-ac15-cdeca9d95cb1")
	)
	(text "NOTES\n- Valve GPIOs come from CONFIG_DYNAMIC_VALVE_GPIO_LIST = 1,14,18,21,22,16,17,5\n  (valves 1-8, CONFIG_DEVICE_MAX_VALVES = 8). All 8 relay channels are valves.\n- GPIO 16/17 are UART0: the console runs on USB Serial/JTAG.\n- No safe GPIO is left: more valves, the 24 VAC converter enable,\n  mains-detect and battery sense need an I2C expander / I2C ADC.\n- Relay contacts are not in the relay module symbol: J2 pin 1 -> COM1..8,\n  NO1..8 -> valves 1..8, J2 pin 2 -> valve common.\n- Power: PS1 holds the +24V bus at 27.6 V and floats BT1+BT2 (via F1, U2).\n  U1 makes +5V. U3 makes 24 VAC for the valves. Mains-detect, battery sense\n  and U3 EN need the I2C expander / ADC (TBD); EN is unconnected for now.\n- IO6/IO7: UART1 link to the ESP32-S3 through J4 (S3 TX -> IO7, IO6 -> S3 RX).\n- The I2C bus uses header pins 28/29; pins 9/10 are the same signals.\n- I2C pull-ups are on the breakout boards.\n  BMP581: SDO=GND (address 0x46), CS=3V3 (I2C mode).\n- 1.8k/3.3k dividers scale the 0-5 V sensor outputs to 0-3.24 V.\n- Not drawn yet: ESP32-S3 (it will drive the LCD2004), I2C expander / ADC."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 76.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e05f14a5-22c6-4c52-b302-19c10c4919ac")
	)
